GET {{onboarding}}/openapi/v1.json


# Section 7. An approved application (not MD, not referred) is handed to the Accounts worker, which opens the account in
# core banking. GET the application (1.3) for ACCOUNT_OPENED, and watch the stand-in with 7.7. Scenario markers in the
# last name: Timeout | Busy | Invalid | Eod. Timings are the Development ones (src/Accounts.Worker/appsettings.Development.json).

### 7.1 Normal: ACCOUNT_OPENED a few seconds after APPROVED
POST {{gateway}}/applications
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: 8c3f7e4a-2d9b-4e3c-9b5a-4f0d6c8e2a71

{
  "firstName": "Ivo", "lastName": "Opening", "dateOfBirth": "1990-06-15",
  "country": "MA", "nationality": "MKD",
  "identifier": { "type": "NATIONAL_ID", "value": "1506990453319" },
  "email": "ivo@example.com", "phone": "+38970123458",
  "documents": [ { "type": "PASSPORT", "image": "aGVsbG8=" }, { "type": "SELFIE", "image": "aGVsbG8=" } ],
  "termsAccepted": true
}

### 7.2 OpenAccount outlives the 20-second timeout but does open the account. Accounts never calls it again: it looks the
#     account up every 15 seconds until the replica shows it (about 80 seconds in), then ACCOUNT_OPENED. One account.
### 7.2 Timeout, reconciled by lookup
POST {{gateway}}/applications
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: 8c3f7e4a-2d9b-4e3c-9b5a-4f0d6c8e2a72

