### 7.7 Core banking stand-in: accounts opened (duplicates must stay empty), calls in flight now and at peak per market
GET {{stubs}}/_stub/corebanking

### 7.8 Reset the stand-in's accounts
DELETE {{stubs}}/_stub/corebanking

### 7.9 Core banking stand-in directly: OpenAccount (SOAP 1.1)
POST {{stubs}}/corebanking/MA/accounts
Content-Type: text/xml
SOAPAction: "urn:cbs:accounts:v3/OpenAccount"

<soap:Envelope xmlns:soap="http://schemas.xmlsoap.org/soap/envelope/" xmlns:acc="urn:cbs:accounts:v3">
  <soap:Body>
    <acc:OpenAccount>
      <acc:FirstName>Ana</acc:FirstName><acc:LastName>Petrova</acc:LastName><acc:DateOfBirth>1991-03-04</acc:DateOfBirth>
      <acc:NationalId>0403991450014</acc:NationalId><acc:ChannelReference>manual-test</acc:ChannelReference>
    </acc:OpenAccount>
  </soap:Body>
</soap:Envelope>

### 7.10 Core banking stand-in directly: FindCustomerAccounts (shows an account 10 seconds after it was opened)
POST {{stubs}}/corebanking/MA/accounts
Content-Type: text/xml
SOAPAction: "urn:cbs:accounts:v3/FindCustomerAccounts"

<soap:Envelope xmlns:soap="http://schemas.xmlsoap.org/soap/envelope/" xmlns:acc="urn:cbs:accounts:v3">
  <soap:Body>
    <acc:FindCustomerAccounts><acc:NationalId>0403991450014</acc:NationalId></acc:FindCustomerAccounts>
  </soap:Body>
</soap:Envelope>


### Section 8. Submissions are limited per client address: 10 per minute (Gateway:RateLimiting in src/Gateway/appsettings.json).
# Run 8.1 eleven times within a minute: the first ten reach Onboarding and fail validation (the body is empty), the eleventh is refused
# before it reaches Onboarding. Every request counts, valid or not. GET requests are not limited.

### 8.1 Run eleven times quickly: the 11th answers 429 with Retry-After
POST {{gateway}}/applications
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: 5e7c2a1b-8d4f-4b3a-9c6e-1f0a2b3c4d81

{}

### 8.2 The counter in Redis (from a terminal):
#     docker exec atlas-redis-1 redis-cli --scan --pattern 'atlas:gateway:ratelimit:*'
#     Turn the limit off for a run: Gateway__RateLimiting__Enabled=false dotnet run --project src/AppHost


# Section 9. Several copies of each service (the stand-ins stay single: they keep their state in memory).
#     dotnet run --project src/AppHost -- --Atlas:Replicas=3
# Then submit several applications (1.1, 7.x; at most 10 a minute from one address, section 8) and look at:
#   - the dashboard: three copies of onboarding-api, verification-worker and accounts-worker;
#   - Seq, grouped by @Resource.service.instance.id: the copies share the messages;
#   - submissions still answer within about 100 ms: the decision may be recorded by one API copy while another holds
#     the request, and the broadcast (ApplicationDecided) wakes whichever holds it;
#   - 9.1: never more than 2 core banking calls in flight per market, however many Accounts workers claim.

### 9.1 Core banking stand-in: peakInFlight stays at 2 per market with three Accounts workers
GET {{stubs}}/_stub/corebanking
